window.docContents[44].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___39-Continued-Fractions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___39-Continued-Fractions--___4___39-Continued-Fractions--Hyperbolic-tangent":{"contents":"The pole set and the finite bottom-up construction are explicit in Lean.  At\ndepth n, tanhTail 0 n z ends at the denominator 2n+3, so the convergent\ncontains exactly the first n+1 odd denominators after the leading 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe DLMF continued fraction is\n\\operatorname{tanh}z=\\frac{z}{1+\\frac{z^2}{3+\\frac{z^2}{5+\\frac{z^2}{7+\\cdots}}}}$$\nfor complex z away from the poles\nz = ±(2m+1)π i/2.  The nth Lean convergent retains the denominator 1\nand then the first n+1 odd denominators beginning with 3; its limit is\nthe canonical complex hyperbolic tangent (A&S 4.5.70).\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.39 Continued Fractions\u0009§4.39 Continued Fractions","header":"Hyperbolic tangent","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___39-Continued-Fractions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___39-Continued-Fractions--___4___39-Continued-Fractions--Hyperbolic-tangent"}});